---
import ProductPageLayout from "../../../layouts/ProductPageLayout.astro";

const structuredData = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	name: "Local Market Capture System",
	serviceType: "Local digital acquisition system",
	provider: {
		"@type": "Organization",
		name: "Intent & Proof",
		url: "https://www.intentandproof.com/"
	},
	description: "A connected local acquisition system combining high-performance web infrastructure, local search visibility, proof, conversion paths and lead measurement.",
	areaServed: "Europe"
};
---

<ProductPageLayout
	title="Local Market Capture System | Intent & Proof"
	description="Build a connected local acquisition system that turns nearby search demand into qualified enquiries through websites, landing pages, local SEO, proof and measurement."
	canonicalPath="/products/local-market-capture-system/"
	noindex={true}
	structuredData={structuredData}
>
	<section class="pp-hero">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-hero__grid">
			<div class="pp-hero__copy">
				<p class="pp-eyebrow">Local digital acquisition product</p>
				<h1>Turn local search demand into qualified enquiries.</h1>
				<p class="pp-hero__intro">
					The Local Market Capture System connects a high-performance website, service and location pages, Google visibility, credible proof, conversion paths and lead measurement into one commercial system.
				</p>
				<div class="pp-hero__actions">
					<a class="pp-button pp-button--primary" href="/diagnostic/">Request a local market diagnostic <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
					<a class="pp-button pp-button--secondary" href="#system">Explore the system</a>
				</div>
				<div class="pp-hero__price">
					<span>Projects from</span>
					<strong>€8,500</strong>
				</div>
				<ul class="pp-hero__meta" aria-label="Product summary">
					<li>8–12 week implementation</li>
					<li>Defined deliverables</li>
					<li>Built around real local demand</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-visual-stage" data-visual-slot="hero-local-market-system">
				<div class="pp-dashboard">
					<div class="pp-dashboard__topbar">
						<div class="pp-dashboard__brand">
							<span class="pp-dashboard__mark">I&amp;P</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Local Market Console</strong>
								<span>Territory, visibility and enquiry performance</span>
							</div>
						</div>
						<span class="pp-dashboard__status"><i></i> Market active</span>
					</div>
					<div class="pp-dashboard__body">
						<div class="pp-map-panel" aria-hidden="true">
							<div class="pp-map-pin pp-map-pin--a"><span>01</span></div>
							<div class="pp-map-pin pp-map-pin--b"><span>02</span></div>
							<div class="pp-map-pin pp-map-pin--c"><span>03</span></div>
							<span class="pp-map-label pp-map-label--a">Primary service area</span>
							<span class="pp-map-label pp-map-label--b">High-value query cluster</span>
							<span class="pp-map-label pp-map-label--c">Expansion opportunity</span>
						</div>
						<div class="pp-insight-panel">
							<h3>Local opportunity</h3>
							<p>A single view of demand, visibility, conversion readiness and lead quality.</p>
							<div class="pp-mini-metric">
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__head"><span>Local visibility</span><strong>78</strong></div>
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__bar"><i style="--pp-bar-width:78%; --pp-bar-color:var(--pp-teal);"></i></div>
							</div>
							<div class="pp-mini-metric">
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__head"><span>Conversion readiness</span><strong>64</strong></div>
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__bar"><i style="--pp-bar-width:64%; --pp-bar-color:var(--pp-cobalt);"></i></div>
							</div>
							<div class="pp-mini-metric">
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__head"><span>Proof strength</span><strong>57</strong></div>
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__bar"><i style="--pp-bar-width:57%; --pp-bar-color:var(--pp-orange);"></i></div>
							</div>
							<div class="pp-mini-metric">
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__head"><span>Measurement integrity</span><strong>72</strong></div>
								<div class="pp-mini-metric__bar"><i style="--pp-bar-width:72%; --pp-bar-color:var(--pp-mint);"></i></div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="pp-lead-card">
					<span class="pp-lead-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
					<div><small>Qualified enquiry</small><strong>Service, location and intent connected</strong></div>
				</div>
				<span class="pp-visual-note">Hero illustration slot · future custom visual</span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-proof-strip" aria-label="Operating evidence">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-proof-strip__grid">
			<div class="pp-proof-item"><strong>#2</strong><span>Priority local search position reached in a live service market.</span></div>
			<div class="pp-proof-item"><strong>100</strong><span>Mobile PageSpeed achieved on deployed acquisition infrastructure.</span></div>
			<div class="pp-proof-item"><strong>2/2</strong><span>First premium enquiries converted in a specialist local market.</span></div>
			<div class="pp-proof-item"><strong>Live</strong><span>Methods tested across local, professional and high-value services.</span></div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-problem-grid">
			<div class="pp-problem-copy">
				<p class="pp-eyebrow">The commercial problem</p>
				<h2>Local visibility fails when the rest of the buying path is weak.</h2>
				<p>
					Ranking, profile activity and website traffic are not the final result. They become commercially useful only when the right buyer reaches a relevant page, finds enough proof, takes a clear action and can be traced into the sales process.
				</p>
				<ul class="pp-problem-list">
					<li>Google Business Profile attracts attention but sends buyers to a generic or slow website.</li>
					<li>Service and location pages exist, but do not match the intent behind valuable searches.</li>
					<li>Reviews and expertise are scattered rather than organised around buyer risk.</li>
					<li>Calls, forms, WhatsApp conversations and bookings are counted without lead-quality context.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-search-preview" data-visual-slot="problem-search-to-conversion">
				<div class="pp-search-bar"><span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span><span>specialist service near me</span></div>
				<div class="pp-search-preview__grid">
					<div class="pp-local-pack">
						<div class="pp-local-pack__map" aria-hidden="true"><i><span>A</span></i><i><span>B</span></i><i><span>C</span></i></div>
						<div class="pp-result-row"><span class="pp-result-row__rank">1</span><div><strong>Relevant local provider</strong><small>Complete profile · strong service match</small></div><span class="pp-result-row__stars">★★★★★</span></div>
						<div class="pp-result-row"><span class="pp-result-row__rank">2</span><div><strong>Generic competitor</strong><small>Weak destination page</small></div><span class="pp-result-row__stars">★★★★</span></div>
					</div>
					<div class="pp-site-card">
						<div class="pp-site-card__window">
							<div class="pp-site-card__browser"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
							<div class="pp-site-card__hero"><span></span><strong></strong><strong></strong><div class="pp-site-card__cta"></div></div>
							<div class="pp-site-card__proof"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
						</div>
						<p class="pp-site-card__caption">The search result and the destination page must tell one coherent commercial story.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="system" class="pp-section pp-section--dark">
		<div class="pp-shell">
			<div class="pp-section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="pp-eyebrow">The connected system</p>
					<h2>Five modules. One local acquisition outcome.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>Each module solves a separate weakness. Together they connect market demand to a measurable qualified enquiry.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-modules-grid">
				<article class="pp-module-card"><span class="pp-module-card__number">01</span><h3>Local Demand Intelligence</h3><p>Identify valuable services, queries, territories, competitors and the order in which the market should be entered.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-module-card"><span class="pp-module-card__number">02</span><h3>High-Performance Local Website</h3><p>Build the technical and commercial foundation around service pages, location architecture and fast mobile performance.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-module-card"><span class="pp-module-card__number">03</span><h3>Google &amp; Map Visibility</h3><p>Align profile, categories, services, location signals and destination pages around relevant local intent.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-module-card"><span class="pp-module-card__number">04</span><h3>Proof &amp; Lead Conversion</h3><p>Resolve buyer risk through reviews, evidence, case material and clear contact or booking paths.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-module-card"><span class="pp-module-card__number">05</span><h3>Measurement &amp; Expansion</h3><p>Connect enquiries to source, quality and outcome before expanding services, locations or advertising spend.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section pp-section--soft">
		<div class="pp-shell">
			<div class="pp-section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="pp-eyebrow">How the product works</p>
					<h2>The page will show the system, not merely describe it.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>The visual frames below are deliberate image positions. They can later be replaced by custom Moz-style illustrations without rebuilding the page structure.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-feature-stack">
				<article class="pp-feature-row">
					<div class="pp-feature-copy">
						<p class="pp-eyebrow">01 · Market architecture</p>
						<h3>Map the demand before producing pages.</h3>
						<p>We define the relationship between services, buyer intent, geography and commercial value before deciding what the site or campaign should contain.</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Service and territory opportunity map</li>
							<li>Priority keyword and entity clusters</li>
							<li>Competitor and local-result analysis</li>
							<li>Phased market-entry plan</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="pp-feature-visual" data-visual-slot="local-demand-intelligence">
						<span class="pp-feature-visual__label">Future illustration · demand map</span>
						<div class="pp-keyword-map" aria-hidden="true">
							<div class="pp-keyword-column"><div class="pp-keyword-chip"><strong>Service intent</strong><span>High commercial relevance</span></div><div class="pp-keyword-chip"><strong>Problem intent</strong><span>Education and qualification</span></div></div>
							<div class="pp-keyword-column"><div class="pp-keyword-chip pp-keyword-chip--core"><strong>Local market</strong><span>Service × place × buyer</span></div></div>
							<div class="pp-keyword-column"><div class="pp-keyword-chip"><strong>Primary territory</strong><span>Immediate demand capture</span></div><div class="pp-keyword-chip"><strong>Expansion territory</strong><span>Validated second phase</span></div></div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<article class="pp-feature-row">
					<div class="pp-feature-copy">
						<p class="pp-eyebrow">02 · Website and conversion</p>
						<h3>Build a destination worthy of the search intent.</h3>
						<p>The website, service pages and landing paths are designed as conversion infrastructure, not as a catalogue of company information.</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Fast, technically sound website foundation</li>
							<li>Service and location page architecture</li>
							<li>Campaign-specific landing pages</li>
							<li>Call, form, WhatsApp or booking paths</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="pp-feature-visual" data-visual-slot="website-and-landing-system">
						<span class="pp-feature-visual__label">Future illustration · website system</span>
						<div class="pp-browser-system" aria-hidden="true">
							<div class="pp-browser-system__bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
							<div class="pp-browser-system__content"><div class="pp-browser-system__copy"><span></span><strong></strong><strong></strong><i></i></div><div class="pp-browser-system__proof"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>

				<article class="pp-feature-row">
					<div class="pp-feature-copy">
						<p class="pp-eyebrow">03 · Measurement and expansion</p>
						<h3>Know which local demand is worth scaling.</h3>
						<p>Visibility is connected to enquiries, lead quality and commercial outcomes so expansion decisions are based on evidence rather than platform activity alone.</p>
						<ul>
							<li>Call, form, booking and WhatsApp tracking</li>
							<li>Lead-source and quality classification</li>
							<li>Local performance dashboard</li>
							<li>Expansion plan for services and territories</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="pp-feature-visual" data-visual-slot="measurement-and-expansion">
						<span class="pp-feature-visual__label">Future illustration · measurement dashboard</span>
						<div class="pp-measurement-board" aria-hidden="true">
							<div class="pp-measurement-board__chart"><strong>Qualified enquiry trend</strong><span>Search visibility connected to outcomes</span></div>
							<div class="pp-measurement-board__metrics"><div class="pp-measurement-board__metric"><span>Qualified lead rate</span><strong>41%</strong></div><div class="pp-measurement-board__metric"><span>Priority territory</span><strong>North zone</strong></div><div class="pp-measurement-board__metric"><span>Next action</span><strong>Expand service cluster</strong></div></div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section">
		<div class="pp-shell">
			<div class="pp-section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="pp-eyebrow">Defined deliverables</p>
					<h2>A product with a concrete scope.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>The final scope depends on the market and current infrastructure, but every project is assembled from clearly defined operating components.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-deliverables-grid">
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">01</span><h3>Market opportunity brief</h3><p>Demand, services, locations, competitors, buyer intent and commercial priorities translated into an implementation sequence.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">02</span><h3>Website architecture</h3><p>Technical structure, service hierarchy, location model, internal links and conversion paths designed before production.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">03</span><h3>Core pages and landing paths</h3><p>High-priority service, location and campaign pages built around search intent, proof and a specific next action.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">04</span><h3>Local visibility foundation</h3><p>Google Business Profile, service and category alignment, local signals, review architecture and destination-page consistency.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">05</span><h3>Proof and conversion system</h3><p>Case material, reviews, authority elements, contact routes and qualification mechanisms organised around buyer risk.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-deliverable-card"><span class="pp-deliverable-card__icon">06</span><h3>Measurement and launch plan</h3><p>Conversion events, lead-source logic, validation checks, reporting and the next expansion decision documented at launch.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section pp-section--dark">
		<div class="pp-shell">
			<div class="pp-section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="pp-eyebrow">Implementation process</p>
					<h2>Diagnose, architect, build, launch and validate.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>A defined sequence keeps strategic decisions separate from production and prevents local expansion from becoming a pile of disconnected pages.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="pp-process">
				<div class="pp-process-step"><span class="pp-process-step__number">01</span><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Evaluate the market, current site, visibility, proof and measurement.</p></div>
				<div class="pp-process-step"><span class="pp-process-step__number">02</span><h3>Architect</h3><p>Define services, territories, page roles and the conversion model.</p></div>
				<div class="pp-process-step"><span class="pp-process-step__number">03</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Produce the website, pages, proof and local infrastructure.</p></div>
				<div class="pp-process-step"><span class="pp-process-step__number">04</span><h3>Launch</h3><p>Publish, connect platforms and test every important action path.</p></div>
				<div class="pp-process-step"><span class="pp-process-step__number">05</span><h3>Validate</h3><p>Review demand, enquiries and quality before scaling the system.</p></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-investment-panel">
			<div class="pp-investment-copy">
				<p class="pp-eyebrow">Investment</p>
				<h2>Built as acquisition infrastructure, not sold as isolated SEO tasks.</h2>
				<p>Projects are scoped around the market, the existing website and the number of services or territories required. The starting investment covers a focused single-market implementation with defined commercial priorities.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pp-investment-card">
				<small>Projects start at</small>
				<strong>€8,500</strong>
				<span>Typical implementation: 8–12 weeks. Multi-location, multilingual and larger market architectures are scoped separately.</span>
				<a class="pp-button pp-button--primary" href="/diagnostic/">Request the diagnostic <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section pp-section--soft">
		<div class="pp-shell">
			<div class="pp-section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="pp-eyebrow">Best suited to</p>
					<h2>Service businesses where local demand has meaningful economic value.</h2>
				</div>
				<p>The system is designed for markets where trust, location and a qualified enquiry matter more than raw traffic volume.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pp-fit-grid">
				<article class="pp-fit-card"><span class="pp-fit-card__tag">Medical</span><h3>Clinics and specialist practices</h3><p>Connect local intent, professional proof and appointment conversion around high-value treatments or services.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-fit-card"><span class="pp-fit-card__tag">Professional</span><h3>Local professional firms</h3><p>Make expertise visible and create a clear path from geographic search to a qualified consultation.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-fit-card"><span class="pp-fit-card__tag">Specialist</span><h3>Technical and premium services</h3><p>Capture narrow, valuable demand where competence and evidence must be understood before price.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-fit-card"><span class="pp-fit-card__tag">Multi-area</span><h3>Businesses expanding territory</h3><p>Build a repeatable local architecture before multiplying locations, pages or advertising spend.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-section">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-faq">
			<div class="pp-faq__intro">
				<p class="pp-eyebrow">Common questions</p>
				<h2>What this product is, and what it is not.</h2>
				<p>The Local Market Capture System is a defined implementation project. It is not an open-ended monthly bundle of unrelated marketing activity.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pp-faq-list">
				<article class="pp-faq-item"><h3>Is this only local SEO?</h3><p>No. Local SEO is one module. The product also addresses the website, destination pages, proof, conversion paths, tracking and lead-quality validation.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-faq-item"><h3>Do we need a new website?</h3><p>Not automatically. The diagnostic determines whether the current infrastructure can support the system or whether rebuilding is more efficient than retrofitting.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-faq-item"><h3>Does the price include advertising spend?</h3><p>No. The implementation investment covers strategy, architecture, production and validation. Media budgets and ongoing platform fees are separate.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-faq-item"><h3>Can the system support several locations?</h3><p>Yes. Multi-location systems require additional data, governance and page architecture, so they are scoped above the single-market starting investment.</p></article>
				<article class="pp-faq-item"><h3>What happens after launch?</h3><p>The initial validation period identifies what should be improved or expanded. Ongoing optimisation can then be defined around evidence rather than assumed activity.</p></article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="pp-final">
		<div class="pp-shell pp-final__panel">
			<div>
				<h2>Map the local opportunity before building more pages or buying more traffic.</h2>
				<p>Start with a diagnostic of the market, current website, proof, conversion paths and measurement.</p>
			</div>
			<a class="pp-button pp-button--primary" href="/diagnostic/">Request a local market diagnostic <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
		</div>
	</section>
</ProductPageLayout>
